{"High-cardinality denial cache key: The denial cache key includes resource name and parent folder, which could create very high cardinality in the cache with many dashboards/folders causing many unique keys. Consider hashing name+parent (e.g., sha256) before adding to the cache key to keep keys compact.": 0.15192456543445587, "Key collision / delimiter ambiguity: The current key-building concatenates fields with '_' and '.' separators, which could accidentally collide if fields themselves contain these characters. Hashing part of the key would address this.": 0.2204538732767105, "Denial cache correctness vs. creator-immediacy: The denial cache can wrongly deny access for a user who just created a resource. When a resource is created, explicitly delete the denial cache key(s) relevant to the creator, or ensure the denial TTL is very short and document the tradeoff.": 0.6316567063331604, "Missing code comments explaining Check flow behavior: In Check, cached 'false' does not imply final deny and DB is rechecked - this behavior should be explicitly commented for future maintainers.": 0.015229242853820324, "Error handling on cache Set is ignored: cache.Set return values/errors are ignored in several places. Consider logging cache set errors if observing cache failures is important.": 0.06239611655473709, "NoopCache should be moved to a separate file (noop_cache.go) or near other cache helpers for clarity.": 0.0035129382740706205, "Missing comment on denial cache explaining TTL semantics and noting it is best-effort and can be evicted/cleared on resource creation if needed.": 0.013582571409642696, "Potential double-counting of metrics: permissionCacheUsage and requestCount are incremented in several places - be careful not to double-count events in some edge flows. Consider adding a test for metrics correctness.": 0.3023926317691803}